    LONG    rgWinEnd
    LONG    bRgCaptured                                     ' the capture was frozen (drain legal, I10)
    LONG    bRgIdleUp                                       ' any captured sample showed the idle wheel up
    ' R18.1: the speed the wheel was holding when this rung was commanded, so BM-RUNGTR carries the
    '  transition's DELTA and its DIRECTION rather than only its destination. Zero means from rest, which
    '  is what a lifetime start and a fault recovery both leave behind -- slotLastIncre is cleared there.
    LONG    rgFromIncre
    LONG    slotLastIncre[INST_MOTORS]                      ' last increment commanded to each motor, 0 at rest
    ' R18.1: the driver's health counters, snapshotted at the command and differenced at each end of the
    '  window. The TRANSITION difference covers the ramp and the settle; the WINDOW difference covers the
    '  steady run. Each is valid only when both of its snapshots were taken.
    LONG    hlCmdLag, hlCmdCap                              ' snapshot at the command
    LONG    bRgHlCmd
    LONG    rgHlTrLag, rgHlTrCap                            ' command -> window start
    LONG    bRgHlTrValid
